<title>USA: Cinergy expects Q3 windfall charge $0.72/shr.</title>
<headline>Cinergy expects Q3 windfall charge $0.72/shr.</headline>
<dateline>CINCINNATI 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cinergy Corp said Thursday it expects to take a one-time charge of approximately $113 million or $0.72 per share in the third quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>Cinergy, which owns a 50 percent stake in Midlands Electricity Plc, said the charge will stem from a windfall profits tax announced by the government of the United Kingdom earlier this month.</p>
<p>It said the charge would be taken in the period during which the legislation is enacted into law, which is expected to be in the third quarter.  Cinergy is the parent of Cincinnati Gas &amp; Electric Co and PSI Energy Inc.</p>
</text>
